    {
      "type": "teach",
      "title": "The schwa hides in plain sight",
      "body": "𐑩 is the sound of an unstressed syllable, so the longer the word, the more of them it holds. In 𐑐𐑻𐑕𐑩𐑯 and 𐑢𐑫𐑥𐑩𐑯 the second vowel is barely there when you say it — and that is exactly what 𐑩 spells. Say each word aloud and listen for the part you almost swallow."
